[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4466"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4}-2}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-2)(\\sqrt{x}+2)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{x-4}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-302322/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "24cf0ad0-ab60-5a30-9ac4-3231c0c94e85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302322/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b6726a7e-b16a-5b7e-9ea4-282df7d3b681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302322/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "686cebf8-b881-5bb8-aaf1-d98b1c24baa1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302322/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-302322/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-302322/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302322" :question/id #uuid "c2769d9a-ddb4-50d7-a6fa-fc81c76cd49c" :question/math-academy-id "q-302322" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x+1}-1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(x+1)-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{x}(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\cancel{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+1}+1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+1}+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-302322/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
